<!--
  Every user-visible string lives here, not as a Kotlin literal in a composable. Beyond the usual
  reason (one place to change copy), this file IS the input to Play Console's free Gemini app-strings
  translation (Grow users → Translations → App strings): Play reads the latest strings.xml out of the
  uploaded bundle and injects the translated resources back in. A literal baked into a composable is
  invisible to it and stays English in every locale, so a hardcoded string is now a shipping bug, not
  a style nit. See docs/guides/localization.md.

  Brand nouns carry translatable="false" so the service leaves them alone.
-->
